## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation for Next.js

### Summary
Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project using the App Router setup.

### Changes Made

#### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics package
- Used npm to install @vercel/analytics package
- Updated package.json with the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with all transitive dependencies

#### 2. Added Analytics component to root layout
**File Modified:** `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after `{children}`
- This ensures analytics tracking is enabled for all pages in the application

### Implementation Details
- The project uses Next.js App Router (version 14.2.5) with TypeScript
- Located the root layout at `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Preserved all existing code structure and styling (Tailwind CSS, fonts, etc.)
- Analytics component is properly placed within the body tag for optimal tracking

### Verification Steps Completed
✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ No ESLint warnings or errors introduced
✅ Package dependencies properly installed and locked
✅ All routes built correctly (7 routes identified)

### Files Modified
1. `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
2. `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependencies
3. `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component

### Notes
- The Analytics component is from @vercel/analytics/next, which is the correct import for Next.js App Router
- No breaking changes to existing functionality
- The component will automatically track web vitals and analytics data
